phase P16
title Test system
description
    **Class:** not readily verifiable.

    **Kind:** verification-suite.

    **Goal:** Flow's own tests run on Flow's own test tooling (Story, Fake, the runtime cut, the trace, the CLI); the
    hand cases are ported onto it and the bridge is deleted. Decided by the user on 2026-11-15; the design and its
    evidence are in code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/test-system-2026-11-15.md.

    **Starts when:** now, ahead of the remaining core slices: @task.V3.T54 waits on @task.V3.T67, and @task.V3.T18
    waits on @task.V3.T69 and @task.V3.T70.

    **Verified by:**

    - the suite: the Story tests under `packages/flow-state-v3/tests/`, with the run rules and the reload sweep, run
      by `vp test`; the builder runs it, and a lead that did not build it audits it
      (skill:policy-testing#audit-a-suite);
    - its mutants: `nub run faults` plants a dead core and each named fault of
      code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/faults.ts in a scratch copy, one at a time;
    - its coverage record: written by @task.V3.T67 and proposed as a verification entry of @plan.Runtime, which is
      a Plan edit and so the user's yes; until then it is a comment on this phase;
    - skill:check-task per Task; `nub run check` and `nub run lint:rules` at zero.

    **One iteration:** the next ready Task: write its checks and see them fail, build, run the suite and
    `nub run faults`, then an independent skill:check-task. Findings are gathered by root cause before the next Task.

    **Exit criteria:**

    - every Task is done, and `tests/bridge/` is deleted, so one test style is left;
    - everything under "Prove" in skill:policy-verification holds at the final revision: the suite runs end to end,
      the dead core and every named fault are caught, and the audit has passed;
    - the coverage record exists.

    **False pass:** a harness made of the product hiding the product's bugs; a ported test that asserts less than
    the case it replaces.

    **Caught by:** the fault run and the dead core; the pure core tests beside the core
    (code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/cells.test.ts); the case-by-case comparison in @task.V3.T67.

    **Gates:**

    - `nub run faults`, which rejects the dead core and the 17 named faults in
      code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/faults.ts;
    - `nub run lint:rules`, which rejects the planted violations in code:tools/flow-state-lint/imports.test.ts and
      code:tools/flow-state-lint/rules.test.ts;
    - `nub run check`.

    **Failure limit:** 2.

    **Stops:**

    - a Pay Story that cannot pass across a reload (@task.V3.T63);
    - public entry-point names (@task.V3.T69);
    - a guarantee change.

    **User's read:** the agent decisions in section 12 of the proposal; the Story and Fake API as built; each case
    the port drops, with its reason.

    **Draws from:**

    - skill:policy-verification (prove a suite; the coverage record);
    - skill:policy-testing (the requirements as failing checks first; audit a suite);
    - skill:execute-task and skill:check-task per Task; skill:review at each Task's close;
    - skill:policy-convergence at the threshold; skill:diagnose when a test fails unexplained;
    - the project's `effect-api-documentation` skill for every Effect API.
tasks
    T62
        title       Package layout and import rules
        status      review
        priority    high
        description
            Fix the package's folders and what may import what, enforced by lint, before the tooling is built.

            **Why now:** tooling, fixtures and tests are about to be written. With no rule, tests reach into `src/`
            and fixtures into tests, which is how the old suite grew a private path to the runtime.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/test-system-2026-11-15.md (section 8 and
            decision 9), code:tools/lint-bomb/FLOW-STATE.md.

            May change: `vite.config.ts`, `tools/flow-state-lint/`, `tools/lint-bomb/FLOW-STATE.md`, AGENTS.md's
            "Where things live". Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a rule that never fires → caught by its planted violation in
            code:tools/flow-state-lint/imports.test.ts.
        acceptance
            - The layout is `src/core/` (pure), `src/host/` (Effect; `src/host/testing/` is the test tooling),
              `fixtures/<name>/`, `tests/<area>/`, `tests/rules/`, `tests/types/` and `bench/`.
            - Lint refuses `src/core/` importing from `src/host/`; `src/` importing a fixture, test or bench; a
              fixture importing from `src/` anything but `src/index.ts` and `src/host/testing/index.ts`; a test or
              bench importing from `src/` anything but those two, `src/host/inspect.ts` and `src/host/trace.ts`.
            - Each rule has a planted violation it refuses and a permitted import it allows.
            - `nub run check`, `nub run lint:rules` and `vp test` pass.
        comment     2026-11-15T09:39:03Z
            Done in commit 087a1b9a: four no-restricted-imports overrides in vite.config.ts, with 20 planted cases in 
            tools/flow-state-lint/imports.test.ts (11 refused, 9 allowed), run by nub run lint:rules. nub run check and 
            vp test pass (262 tests). Today's code already complied, so nothing moved.
    T63
        title       A Story drives the real Runtime over fakes
        status      open
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T62]
        description
            Build `Story`, `Fake` and the run in `src/host/testing/`, with a runtime cut in `src/host/inspect.ts`,
            proven on a transfers fixture and one Pay Story.

            **Why now:** Flow's own tests are to run on its public test tooling, and nothing in production code scripts
            a run or stands in for a service. This is the first slice of @plan.Testing.O1 to O4; @task.V3.T29 keeps the
            rest.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/test-system-2026-11-15.md (sections 3.1, 4, 5,
            7 and 12), code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/host/runtime.ts#buildRuntime,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/fixtures/pay/contracts.ts#ShopApi. Prior art: the local branch
            `draft/story-slice` holds a working spike and an unfinished, unreviewed draft of this Task. Read it; do not
            merge it.

            **Risk:** Pay's commit runs on a detached fiber, and what it does when its page is abandoned at a reload
            is unproven. The second risk is types: a fake must keep each service method's argument, success and
            failure types end to end, with no cast.

            **Approach:** one page is one task list drained to idle (Effect's `Scheduler.MixedScheduler`), one
            `TestClock` and one Runtime; a reload abandons the page and boots another over the same store and fake
            state. Every Effect API is checked against the installed source with the `effect-api-documentation` skill.

            May change: `src/host/testing/`, `src/host/inspect.ts`, `fixtures/transfers/`, `fixtures/pay/server.ts`,
            `fixtures/pay/stories.ts`, `tests/transfers/`, `tests/pay/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a run that ends with work still queued, or tests that pass on a dead core → caught by the idle
            check after every step and by `nub run faults`.
            Gates: `nub run faults` over the new tests, which rejects the dead core.
            Stops: the Pay Story cannot pass across a reload without bending the Runtime. Then the reload model is
            wrong.
            User's read: the Story and Fake API as built, and each place it differs from the proposal's section 4.
        acceptance
            - `Story.app(config, fakes, steps)` is inert data and `run()` is the only boundary. Steps: attach, detach,
              forget, send, disposeActor, disposeRuntime, advance, reload, checkpoint.
            - `Fake.server(Service, () => handlers)` answers through the service's own methods. Its words `hold`,
              `release`, `dropRequest`, `dropResponse` and `answer` are typed by the service. The fake store has
              `hold`, `refuse` and `release`.
            - A checkpoint holds the time, the runtime cut, what each fake received and the store.
            - Every step word and every wire and storage word has a test. A Story run twice gives equal evidence. A
              run arms no host timer. A dead page writes nothing after a reload.
            - The transfers fixture is one folder (contracts, machine, server, stories) with Story tests.
            - One Pay Story passes: a `confirm` whose response is lost, time past the commit's deadline, a reload; the
              payment reads unknown and exactly one `confirm` landed.
            - `nub run faults` over the new tests: a dead core fails every one.
            - An idiomatic-Effect review by a second Opus agent, using `effect-api-documentation`, leaves no finding
              open without a reason.
            - `vp test`, `nub run check` and `nub run lint:rules` pass.
    T64
        title       Rules checked on every run, and a reload at every step
        status      open
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T63]
        description
            Write the run rules and the reload sweep in `tests/rules/`.

            **Why now:** example tests check only what someone wrote down: the planted fault `refused-turn-reported`
            passes all 81 hand cases. The old suite's crash sweep, a kill and reload at every step, found three real
            bugs and was deleted with it.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/test-system-2026-11-15.md (sections 3.2, 3.3
            and 6), code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/faults.ts, and
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/bridge/checks/publication.ts for an older check's logic.

            May change: `tests/rules/`, and the Story tests that call the helper. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a rule that never fires → each rule is shown red on one planted fault.
            Gates: `nub run faults`, which rejects all 17 named faults in code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/faults.ts.
        acceptance
            - A rule is a function from a finished run to its breaches, named by its Spec id. One helper applies every
              rule to a run, and every Story test calls it.
            - The rules: an Attempt's ending is delivered at most once (WriteLanes I15, I16); every ending has one of
              the three channels and a never-sent Attempt ends only NotSent (WriteLanes I3); every request of one
              Attempt carries one idempotency key and one input (WriteLanes I6); at most one publication per turn
              (Turn I9); a refused turn leaves no Turn report (Turn I14).
            - The reload sweep runs every fixture story with a reload inserted at each position and applies the rules.
              A variant fails only for a rule breach, never for a script reason.
            - `nub run faults` catches all 17 named faults.
    T65
        title       A run prints as a text trace
        status      open
        priority    medium
        blocked_by  [@T63]
        description
            Write `src/host/trace.ts`: one function from a finished run to plain text, showing each step, what it
            caused and each checkpoint.

            **Why now:** builders debugged the old suite with private scratch scripts, and a ruling is to be asked as
            two traces of one Story. This is the first slice of @plan.Inspection.O4; @task.V3.T49 keeps the rest.

            May change: `src/host/trace.ts`, `tests/transfers/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a trace that leaves out what a step caused → caught by a snapshot that shows each request,
            ending and store write of a run with a lost answer.
        acceptance
            - The trace of a transfers run matches a text snapshot (`toMatchFileSnapshot`).
            - Two runs of one Story print the same trace.
    T66
        title       The bench times the long stories
        status      open
        priority    medium
        blocked_by  [@T63]
        description
            Write `bench/run.ts`: it runs each fixture's long story a fixed number of times and prints the median and
            p99 time per run and per turn.

            **Why now:** the old bench replayed scripts through the deleted suite. @task.V3.T35 needs something to
            grow from.

            May change: `bench/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a bench that does less work than the tested run → caught by the same-turns test.
        acceptance
            - `bun packages/flow-state-v3/bench/run.ts` prints its numbers for the transfers long story.
            - A test shows the benched Story does the same turns as a tested run of it.
            - Nothing gates on a timing.
    T67
        title       The hand cases run as Story tests and the bridge is gone
        status      open
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T63, @T64]
        description
            Port the 81 cases under `tests/bridge/cases/` to Story tests by Spec area, and delete the bridge.

            **Why now:** two test styles in one tree is how a private harness comes back. Core work
            (@task.V3.T54) waits on this.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/test-system-2026-11-15.md (section 5 and
            Appendix A), code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/bridge/cases/write-lanes/payment-endings.test.ts.

            **Approach:** the pay, cells, sync and sign-in fixtures in the four-file shape first. Then one Spec area
            per commit, each commit deleting the bridge files it replaces. The ten long scripts on the branch
            `draft/story-slice` (under `draft/workloads/`) become each fixture's usual and long stories.

            May change: `fixtures/`, `tests/`, `vite.config.ts` (the bridge's lint exemption). Evidence: this Task's
            comments.

            False pass: a ported test that asserts less than its case did → caught by comparing asserted values case
            by case, and by `nub run faults`.
        acceptance
            - Every bridge case has a Story test asserting the same values; a case dropped is listed with its reason.
            - `tests/bridge/` and `fixtures/part.ts` are deleted, and lint's bridge exemption with them.
            - The five known bugs that have a reproduction (Appendix A) are inverted tests, each titled by the rule it
              breaks.
            - Each fixture has a usual and a long story.
            - `nub run faults`: all 17 faults caught, and a dead core fails every test that is not inverted.
            - The suite's coverage record (Covers, Suite, Rerun, Mutants, Audit, Matched at, Scope, as
              skill:policy-verification gives them) is a comment on this phase, proposed to the user as a
              verification entry of @plan.Runtime.
            - An audit by a lead that did not build the suite (skill:policy-testing#audit-a-suite) has passed.
    T68
        title       Compile-time tests for the type promises production keeps
        status      open
        priority    medium
        description
            Write `tests/types/`: one `@ts-expect-error` test for each "is a type error" promise in the Plans and
            @spec.Compile that production has built.

            **Why now:** the Plans and @spec.Compile make 31 such promises, and 5 checks exist. No run can show a
            type error.

            May change: `tests/types/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a directive that suppresses a different error → each test's line holds only the forbidden
            use.
        acceptance
            - Each promise production has built has a test, and `nub run check` fails when its directive is unused.
            - The promises production has not built are listed in this Task's comments with their owner Task.
    T69
        title       flow story and flow trace
        status      open
        priority    medium
        blocked_by  [@T65]
        description
            Build `flow story list`, `flow story run` and `flow trace <story>`, thin over the run and the trace
            printer.

            **Why now:** a builder's debug loop and a ruling both need a run printed from the command line. This is the
            first slice of @plan.CommandLine.O2; @task.V3.T29 keeps the rest.

            **Risk:** where the CLI lives and how it finds stories are not designed. The Testing plan's `defineConfig`
            discovery is outside this slice.

            False pass: a command that prints through a path of its own → caught by its output equalling the trace
            of @task.V3.T65 for the same Story.
            Stops: public entry-point names.
        acceptance
            - Each command prints from the same run and printer as @task.V3.T65, over the package's fixtures.
            - Each command's output has a text snapshot test.
    T70
        title       Generated Stories
        status      open
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T64]
        description
            Build `propertyTest` in `src/host/testing/`: it generates Stories from a fixture's step samples and the
            fakes' open calls, applies the run rules, shrinks a failure and prints it as a Story.

            **Why now:** nothing generated is left after the old suite's deletion, and @task.V3.T18 brings new
            behaviour. This is the first slice of @plan.Testing.O6.

            **Read first:** @plan.Testing.O6, code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/test-system-2026-11-15.md
            (section 6).

            May change: `src/host/testing/`, `tests/generated/`, `fixtures/` (step samples). Evidence: this Task's
            comments.

            False pass: a generator that only makes Stories the rules cannot fail → caught by finding a planted fault
            from a seed.
        acceptance
            - The same seed gives the same Stories.
            - A planted fault is found from a seed and shrunk to under ten steps, and the failure prints as a Story to
              paste into a fixture.
            - Nothing generated is stored.
            - It runs over every fixture in `tests/generated/`.
